task.description:
Implement the APPROVED design at src/design/iss0629-tc-lua-10-03-flake-fix.md (PASSed CODE-DESIGN-VALIDATOR at commit fb1467f). Small, test-only fix for GH-600: replace TC-LUA-10-03's line 600 (`try std.testing.expect(watchdog_state.hasFired());`) in src/lua/limiter_wiring_test.zig with a bounded 1000ms yield-spin retry loop:

```zig
const retry_deadline = milliTimestamp() + 1_000;
while (!watchdog_state.hasFired() and milliTimestamp() < retry_deadline) {
    std.Thread.yield() catch {};
}
try std.testing.expect(watchdog_state.hasFired());
```

No production code changes (src/lua/timeout.zig untouched). This is the ONLY change needed per the design's scope confirmation (TC-LUA-10-01, TC-LUA-10-02, and TC-LUA-10-03's own mutation-check test do not share this race).

VALIDATION: since this fixes a FLAKY (intermittent) test, a single clean run does not prove the fix worked -- run zig build test-lua MULTIPLE times (at least 5, ideally 10) to build confidence the flake is genuinely resolved, not just that you got lucky once. The original issue observed 3 fail / 2 pass across 5 runs before the fix -- you need enough repeated clean runs after the fix to be reasonably confident the race window is actually closed, not just narrowed.
